{"name":"Sliding","hex":"#97aeaf","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sliding","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of slide"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The motion of something that slides.","skeleton (winter sport)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sliding"}],"entries":[{"title":"Slide (baseball)","blocks":[{"text":"In baseball, a slide is the action of a player, acting as a baserunner, who drops his body to the ground once he is very close to the base he is approaching and slides along the ground to reach the base. Sliding is widely considered to be an essential component of baserunning in both baseball and softball."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Ronald_Acuna_%2850337465807%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Ronald_Acuna_%2850337465807%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Slide_(baseball)"},{"title":"Sliding (motion)","blocks":[{"text":"Sliding is a type of motion between two surfaces in contact. This can be contrasted to rolling motion. Both types of motion may occur in bearings."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sliding_(motion)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Navy_baseball.jpg/500px-Navy_baseball.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Navy_baseball.jpg/1280px-Navy_baseball.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Navy_baseball.jpg/500px-Navy_baseball.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A shortstop attempts to tag out a player sliding head-first into a base","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANavy_baseball.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia